Package term for Radix (ADR 0600): its terminals take Linux's TCGETS and
TCSETS through golang.org/x/sys/unix, as Linux's do.

go.mod names Go 1.22 and requires nothing: Radix's golang.org/x/sys
takes the place of every version of that module, so that a program
whose go.mod names an older Go, or an older x/sys, may take this one in
place of any version of x/term.

diff -ruN a/golang.org_x_term@v0.48.0/go.mod b/golang.org_x_term@v0.48.0/go.mod
--- a/golang.org_x_term@v0.48.0/go.mod
+++ b/golang.org_x_term@v0.48.0/go.mod
@@ -1,5 +1,7 @@
 module golang.org/x/term
 
-go 1.26.0
-
-require golang.org/x/sys v0.50.0
+// Radix: the oldest Go whose language this code builds with, in place of
+// the newest it was released for, and no requirement of golang.org/x/sys,
+// which Radix's takes the place of at every version: a program that names
+// an older Go, or an older x/sys, may take it (ADR 0600).
+go 1.22
diff -ruN a/golang.org_x_term@v0.48.0/term_unix.go b/golang.org_x_term@v0.48.0/term_unix.go
--- a/golang.org_x_term@v0.48.0/term_unix.go
+++ b/golang.org_x_term@v0.48.0/term_unix.go
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 // Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style
 // license that can be found in the LICENSE file.
 
-//go:build aix || darwin || dragonfly || freebsd || linux || netbsd || openbsd || solaris || zos
+//go:build aix || darwin || dragonfly || freebsd || linux || netbsd || openbsd || radix || solaris || zos
 
 package term
 
